																	<a href="/forum/t-13896141/scp-idea:retroactive-weight-gain-supplement#post-4839246">Re: SCP idea:  Retroactive weight gain supplement</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ethanhanson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4465845); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4465845&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607394278" alt="EthanHanson" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4465845)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ethanhanson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4465845); return false;" >EthanHanson</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607393164 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Dec 2020 02:06</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13896141/scp-idea:retroactive-weight-gain-supplement">SCP idea:  Retroactive weight gain supplement</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839246">
									

<p>Let's see what we have here.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>you start to gain memories from before you were born of being something not human.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This part seems to appear out of the blue. Like, you have all these properties about weight loss and then you mention this. What does this have to do with the rest of the concept? I mean, you can add a depth meaning to the pills thing, but you need to have some kind of build-up, not just making it to appear spontaneously.</p>
<p>That said, I think some kind of twist like that would be interesting. The anomaly itself is pretty basic, and I think something like this would help a lot to improve it. What are these &quot;new memories&quot; about? What's the meaning of these memories? Maybe some kind of being wanted us to remember them? Maybe that being created the pills in order to attract us by using a common human desire? If you focus on this part, I think your article would be very interesting.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I haven't decided yet how much it affects other people's memories</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think other people's memories would be unaffected. Like, maybe they just don't want to hurt the subject's feelings? Maybe the subject's in denial about what others say? This is a common effect of real eating disorders, so it would make this concept to feel somewhat realistic.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>or physical records like pictures.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Like I said, maybe they're just in denial of these records? Or maybe they see the records in a different manner?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I haven't decided yet what happens if you stop taking the pills, though it probably depends on if you have passed the critical point or not.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe if they stop eating the pills, the memories slowly start to get back to normal? Maybe they forget about eating the pills in the first place? Maybe they start to have some kind of side effects? Perhaps the pills are like a drug?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I think that you should add some kind of backstory to the existence of the pills.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

							</div>

								
					
