<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> mainly mystery, slight comedy,</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Aiming to make it as short and simple as I can</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A Class-D claims to be an 05-14, no proof of him being an 05, but there is mystery as how he got this way.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> There is a Class-D who claims to be an 05 council member. Due to little evidence supporting him, and a history supporting him being a Class-D, they do not make him an 05. However, they do not terminate him at the end of the month and make him a SCP because he knows stuff only an 05 knows.<br />
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> At the end of the SCP in an addendum, the site director says something like, &quot;We do not know for certain that he is an 05 despite him having classified information. He could be an attempt at infiltration by a GoI, a Class-D who anomalously got his hands on classified information and is attempting to avoid end-of-the-month termination. Maybe he actually is 05-14 and was placed as a Class-D. We really do not know anything about him, and it is much safer to simply contain him than to blindly trust any assumptions. Rest assured, we are investigating this.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> If I manage to fit it in somehow, I can imply that some sort of group inside the Foundation intend to put him back up into the 05 council. As in, maybe some guard slips him a note saying that he believes him, and intends to break him out/investigate it himself. Also, apologies for any mistakes I make, this is my first post ever on the site and I really want to start writing an article after lurking for a couple of years.</p>

