<p>Let's see what we have here.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>he ends up risking up the veil and getting the community he so much loved killed</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What happened? What did he do? I'm guessing it has something to do with the memetic agent. Did they all start to feel the 'bad' effects? Did he try to improve the feelings of his music? Also, why did he get persecuted? You're being very ambiguous with this part; I think you should explain this a little more in order to understand the exact things that happened.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>he releases the memetic agent with ambiguous motivations.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why did he release it? What was he thinking? Was he sad, angry, impulsive&#8230;? I don't see any motive to release the agent on a global scale. I think you should explain his motives in your concept post; even if they're going to be ambiguous in the article, you should have them clear in your mind.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>is it really better to live on your knees than to die on your feet?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What? When did that dilemma come to be? Why is it a part of the story? It seems to appear out of the blue, and I don't see any connection with the story about a guy trying to improve his music. How are you going to portray this in your article?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Is the Foundation really willing to declare a war on artistic expression for the greater good?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What? What happened in order for the Foundation to declare open war on something? Did the agent get out of control? What happened to the world? You didn't say anything about this part in your concept.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I think your concept is missing some key points regarding the story you're planning to tell.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

