														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839210">
									

<p>Let's see what we have here.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The pocket dimension is something like a paradise version of the original forest clearing</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think you should explain a little more on this. What do you mean by 'paradise'? What's different from the real forest? You can play with the descriptions and/or physics of the pocket dimension. I think you should try to make the reader into 'feel' the sensation of what is like to be there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>in the middle of the forest clearing is an old ruin</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Who lived there? Why no one lives there anymore? You can play with this. What was life like in there? You can have a lot of worldbuilding here. Maybe you can use it to show how a civilization living in &quot;paradise&quot; rose and fell? Maybe you can make this a metaphor of utopias and their inevitable collapse?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the portal got unstable and is now neutralized</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This part could also be a metaphor about &quot;dream places&quot; being destined to collapse. This would be a nice and simple ending to a good story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the will to stay in the pd grows with the time</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe, along with the pd, the traces of the civilization also grow? This way your story will have some type of escalation through the article. Maybe you could write one exploration log about a D-Class going in there and being happy while discovering the place's history?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>if anyone tries to force someone to exit the pd after they spent more than 13 min in it, they'll do everything just to stay there</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So how did the person who got lost even get out? I think they would've never leave, just because they would've not feel the necessity to do so. I think you should either get rid of this property, or came up with another story regarding its discovery. Maybe some disappearances? Maybe a group of friends find it and one of them got inside and didn't want to exit?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, you have the opportunity to do a lot of worldbuilding here, and I think that would improve your article.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

							</div>

								
					
