														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839204">
									

<p>1) The reviewers are major sticklers on the 400-word limit. Also, you're going to need to collapse it down using the following string: [G[collapsible]G] collapsed text [G[/collapsible]G] (just eliminate the Gs and put a lot of text in place of the &quot;collapsed text&quot; part (check the <strong>wiki text quick reference</strong> under the box for more information).</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>2) The big problem you have is that Coyote has already escaped into the metanarrative in the real world (he's featured in the White Wolf Werewolf: The Apocalypse as a major spirit as well as a number of webcomics and other media, such as the American Gods books and even Marvel Comics). It's hard to keep a good trickster contained.</p>
<p>3) Keep in mind also that as a trickster, and one that's been doing it for aeons, Coyote will find a loophole, assuming it's not a bluff to keep attention over here as he does something over there. Out of all of the various deities you could mess with, this is one of the trickier ones simply because Coyote is known for his schemes.</p>
<p>Ironically, that makes him a good pick for this, but there has to be a reason for him to behave other than his personal honor.</p>
<p>4) This would be better for Tales than as an article. Also, I'm sort of worried about the &quot;tragic&quot; tag; Coyote just doesn't do tragedy. He generally comes out on top and making fun of all of those involved, sometimes even himself. That The Foundation has handled gods is worth noting, especially in this case.</p>
<p>5) The Chaos Insurgency and Serpent's Hand are mutually antagonistic, both between themselves and The Foundation. While it appears that's allowed for with CI, it's unlikely that SH would help The Foundation. Also, as SH hates to contain entities, especially humanoid ones, I'm not sure that they would agree to do so themselves, especially one as potentially powerful as Coyote.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>6) Overall, I think you may be trying to do too much with this, and you may want to break it down a little. You have a couple of different things going on, and any one of them (sapient stories, a character from myth, even a deity branching out) would be great to focus on. I'm just not sure one entry would do it justice.</p>

							</div>

								
					
