			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839202">
									

<p>A book containing all the records set by any entity in any dimension in all of existence. (SCP version of Guinness world records but a multiversal edition)</p>
<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: Tale</p>
<p>Genre: Drama/Emotional, Comedy,</p>
<p>Page Layout: Standard</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: The vehement struggle of a researcher coming to terms with the &quot;record&quot; his father holds.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: A researcher is tasked to read through the book containing countless records. Through fan post/mails send from all over the universes, he comes to learn that his idol, his father, is not the man he had imagined him to be. The book itself has no other anomalous qualities then depicting the records.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: I think that the premise, of a record book in a world full of extremes, is an interesting idea and something which would draw a lot of attention, provided it is done in a sufficient manner. Many parallels to existing SCPs could be drawn as well. The conflict with the unspeakable atrocity the father might have committed should serve as the main point of interest.</p>
<p>-Whatever crime the father has committed will not be mentioned-</p>
<p>After a lengthy discussion on the critters forum, I came to the conclusion, that this idea is better suited for a tale. It is just a revisited idea of an older idea of mine here is a link to it <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13137282/scp-idea-a-multidimensional-book-about-records">http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13137282/scp-idea-a-multidimensional-book-about-records</a></p>
<p>And this is a modernized version of the first thread I had written about the tale idea. Back then, the idea was not fleshed out enough. link <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13675691/a-multidimensional-book-about-records#post-4759034">http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13675691/a-multidimensional-book-about-records#post-4759034</a></p>
<p>I do hope that it now is better suited for the said endeavour.</p>

